// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/test-waves.t27 -- test waves: a t27 spec's test block, simulated and drawn as waves
; Source of truth for public/widgets/test-waves/ (gHashTag/trinity, apps/website). The page is
; written by scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs from this file; tool.js holds no English of its
; own and reads every word below from window.T27_WIDGET.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DRAWS: a timing diagram of one real simulation. The vendored compiler
; (public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm, the one the X player runs) generates Verilog from
; specs/ternary/stream_ternary_mac.t27, a clocked ternary multiply-accumulate. The four vectors
; of that spec's own test blocks, assert_eq(dot27(a, b), d), are streamed into the generated
; module one per clock by scripts/widget-data/test-waves-tb.v under Icarus Verilog (iverilog,
; then vvp); after each edge acc must equal the running sum of the expected dot products. Two
; more checks read the generated RTL: en low holds acc, and rst_n low clears it at once.

; PROVENANCE: scripts/widget-data/test-waves.mjs runs the whole chain and writes demo.vcd, the
; VCD exactly as vvp dumped it, and demo.json: the spec and compiler sha256, the iverilog and
; vvp versions, the exact commands, and the pass or fail of every check. The tool shows all of
; it under the diagram, so a number on the screen can be traced to the command that made it.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that the module was placed, routed or run on a board; this is a
; simulation of generated RTL. That every t27 spec simulates: many generated modules are refused
; by iverilog today (one calls an undeclared cast(), t27#6100), and this one was picked because
; it is accepted and its tests carry vectors. The VCD parser here is small and reads the common
; subset (scalars, vectors, reals as text); a file outside it is refused with a reason, not
; guessed at. A dropped file is read with FileReader in the reader's browser and sent nowhere.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

